==========================================================================================================================
1  SETUP, and the CLIPPING CODE FACT
==========================================================================================================================
  state.extension_scale(eff_state, gaps) returns  1.0 - EXTENSION_STEP * votes  -- there is NO clip at zero.
    STEP = 1/3, 3 votes -> extension_scale = +0.0000   (fine: the A row is 100% cash)
    STEP = 0.5, 3 votes -> extension_scale = -0.5000   NEGATIVE.
    target_weights_with_voltarget('A', ..., gaps={100:.5,150:.5,200:.5}) then returns
      (core -0.250, tqqq -0.250, qld -0.000, xlu -0.000, cash +1.500)  sum 1.000
    state.validate_weights on that tuple -> WeightSanityError: core_weight=-0.25 out of [0,1] range for state A
  CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly and verified above:
    (i)  this test harness CLIPS the multiplier at 0 (mults() above), so the 0.5 arm's 3-vote rung is the intended all-cash row;
    (ii) ADOPTING 0.5 would require a one-line clip in state.py FIRST (e.g. max(0.0, 1.0 - EXTENSION_STEP * votes)).
         Without it the live trigger calls validate_weights*, that raises, and the trigger ABORTS (report, do not trade)
         on every 3-vote day -- i.e. it would not trade the intended cash row, it would fail to trade at all.
    (iii) at STEP 1/3 the expression never goes negative (3 votes x 1/3 = 1.0 exactly), which is why no clip exists today.

  ARMS (A row core/TQQQ/cash at 0 / 1 / 2 / 3 extension votes; the vol target multiplies on top, as live):
    STEP 1/3 (LIVE)  multipliers 1.000/0.667/0.333/0.000   rows (50.0,50.0,0.0) / (33.3,33.3,33.3) / (16.7,16.7,66.7) / (0.0,0.0,100.0)
    STEP 0.5         multipliers 1.000/0.500/0.000/0.000   rows (50.0,50.0,0.0) / (25.0,25.0,50.0) / (0.0,0.0,100.0) / (0.0,0.0,100.0)
    (0.5 is deeper at 1 vote, and reaches full cash at 2 votes instead of 3. Rung 0 is identical in both.)

